  "id": "COMPOUND:1906 - PROTEIN:5740",
  "verbalization": "Staurosporine exerts its biological effects by targeting specific proteins that are involved in cellular processes critical to cancer progression. The evidence suggests that staurosporine interacts with two distinct targets: Cytochrome P450 2E1 and LIM domain kinase 2, both of which are targeted by flavopiridol. Flavopiridol, in turn, has a broad effect on a panel of 60 carcinoma cell lines, indicating a potential role in the treatment of various cancers. This relationship is further supported by the fact that both targets are engaged by flavopiridol, which may modulate the activity of the cell lines in a manner that is relevant to cancer therapy. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential of staurosporine and flavopiridol as agents that influence the cellular environment of carcinoma cell lines, possibly through the modulation of metabolic and signaling pathways. The evidence underscores the importance of targeting these proteins in the context of cancer treatment, though the exact mechanisms by which flavopiridol affects the Panel NCI-60 remain to be fully elucidated.",
